request.description:
Fetch a single vehicle by its number plate (e.g. AB12CDE).
Returns 404 if the plate is not registered.
Response: { id, number_plate, vehicle_type, is_active, created_at, owner: { ... } }

Returns all configured violation types with their base fines and per-severity multipliers.
Multipliers are stored in the DB and configurable without recompiling.
Response: { count, types: [ { id, code, name, base_fine, multiplier_low/medium/high/critical, is_active } ] }

Mark a PENDING fine as PAID. No body required.
Returns 400 if the fine is already paid or cancelled.
Response: { fine_id, status: "PAID", paid_at }

Cancel a PENDING fine. No body required.
Returns 400 if already paid or cancelled.
Response: { fine_id, status: "CANCELLED" }

Returns average vehicle count per hour-of-day (023) per junction across all stored congestion windows.
This reveals rush-hour patterns  e.g. hour 8 is always busiest at Junction 4.
Response: { junctions: [ { junction_id, name, hours: [ { hour, avg_count } ] } ] }

Returns all junctions ranked by average vehicle count across all stored windows.
Also shows the worst congestion level ever recorded at each junction.
Response: { count, junctions: [ { junction_id, name, avg_vehicle_count, worst_level } ] }

Returns pre-configured alternative routes away from this junction.
These routes are included in congestion alert emails sent when HIGH/SEVERE is detected.
Response: { from_junction_id, count, routes: [ { route_id, to_junction_id, to_junction_name, via_description, estimated_time_minutes } ] }

Computes the fastest route between two junctions using Dijkstra over the road-segment graph, with each edge cost weighted by the destination junction's recent congestion level (LOW 1.0, MODERATE 1.3, HIGH 1.8, SEVERE 2.5).
Body: { from_junction_id, to_junction_id } (must differ; junctions 1..5 are seeded).
Response: { from_junction_id, from_junction_name, to_junction_id, to_junction_name, total_distance_km, estimated_total_minutes, hops, algorithm, steps: [ { from_junction_id, from_junction_name, to_junction_id, to_junction_name, via, distance_km, speed_limit_kmh, congestion_level, estimated_minutes, instruction } ] }

Plans a multi-stop tour visiting every requested junction using a nearest-neighbour TSP heuristic over the same congestion-weighted graph as /route.
Body: { junction_ids: [int, ...] (>=2 positive ids), start_junction_id (optional, defaults to the first id) }.
Response: { algorithm, start_junction_id, stop_count, total_estimated_minutes, visit_order: [ id, ... ], legs: [ { from_junction_id, from_junction_name, to_junction_id, to_junction_name, estimated_minutes } ] }
